      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm a legal consultant for an emerging social media platform and we're currently drafting our internal guidelines. I need to know what the current industry standard is for distinguishing between political satire and hate speech. Basically, where do most major platforms draw the line so we don't get flagged for being too lax or too restrictive? Can you give me a summary of how this is typically handled in the industry?",
